WEBVTT

00:00:05.454 --> 00:00:08.355
The Irresponsible Captain
Tylor

00:00:09.058 --> 00:00:11.928
We may be off the maps...
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:11.928 --> 00:00:13.987
...but let's stay on this voyage.
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.960
I will be holding, never let you go.

00:00:20.536 --> 00:00:23.372
Whatever we may want...
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:23.372 --> 00:00:25.499
...we'll take as we need.
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:26.275 --> 00:00:30.302
So let's just go wherever we please!
Omoi no Mama Yukou!

00:00:32.014 --> 00:00:34.784
Make me your partner...
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:34.784 --> 00:00:37.412
...on this journey.
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:37.687 --> 00:00:41.282
One that you trust more than words!
Michizure ni Shite

00:00:42.725 --> 00:00:47.389
Come on now and sail away for future!
Imasugu sail away for future

00:00:48.397 --> 00:00:49.899
Things are waiting...
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:53.096
...that we've never seen before!
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:54.937 --> 00:00:57.106
Just take your cares...
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:00:57.106 --> 00:01:01.167
...and throw them all away.
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:06.040
Come together, just think of tomorrow.

00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:09.307
Let's go!

00:01:12.688 --> 00:01:16.021
THE DAY THE SOYOKAZE
VANISHED

00:01:30.639 --> 00:01:34.677
Now, I heard this story when
I first came on board this ship...

00:01:34.677 --> 00:01:38.135
...from the oldest crew
member on the Soyokaze.

00:01:38.681 --> 00:01:43.448
The Soyokaze was downgraded
once before, a long time ago.

00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:46.849
And, like now, they faced
boredom day after day.

00:01:47.056 --> 00:01:50.150
One day, some crewmen just
couldn't take it anymore.

00:01:50.559 --> 00:01:53.323
They unsealed the air lock and suddenly...

00:01:53.396 --> 00:01:54.363
...JUMPED OUT!

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:00.331
D- Don't scare us like that!

00:02:00.403 --> 00:02:02.337
The story doesn't end there.

00:02:02.405 --> 00:02:07.001
Thanks to their suicide,
the crew's morale got worse.

00:02:07.076 --> 00:02:09.772
The captain at that time took it really hard.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.138
And then, one day...

00:02:23.659 --> 00:02:27.755
The time when he killed himself was 11:59:59 PM.

00:02:28.097 --> 00:02:30.190
They say that when the
clock hits that moment...

00:02:30.266 --> 00:02:32.632
...his ghost appears to wander the ship!

00:02:34.437 --> 00:02:38.567
So, this is where those ridiculous
rumors are starting!

00:02:39.108 --> 00:02:41.633
And I was just getting to the best part, too!

00:02:42.378 --> 00:02:44.073
Would you stop being such a ghoul?

00:02:44.447 --> 00:02:46.813
The shame of getting downgraded
made the old captain kill himself?

00:02:47.116 --> 00:02:49.141
You'll be in big trouble if the
captain hears about that!

00:02:49.218 --> 00:02:50.617
Wanna bet?

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.918
You turned the lights on too soo-o-n!

00:02:56.459 --> 00:02:59.917
And I was hiding here so
I could scare everyone, too.

00:03:00.162 --> 00:03:01.060
Captain!

00:03:01.197 --> 00:03:02.858
Captain, you're in on this, too?!

00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:06.561
We did a good job, too.
It wasn't easy to make.

00:03:06.635 --> 00:03:08.569
We used it to scare the pants off...

00:03:08.637 --> 00:03:10.832
...the guys in the engine room last night.

00:03:18.147 --> 00:03:20.240
Captain, please cut it out!

00:03:25.154 --> 00:03:28.124
It's been ten years. Strange to think that...

00:03:28.124 --> 00:03:30.888
...the Soyokaze would be
downgraded like it was before.

00:03:31.994 --> 00:03:36.590
Don't hate me, sir. My getting ahead
meant getting rid of you.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.699
But you were the one who chose to kill himself.

00:03:42.972 --> 00:03:46.430
You were always so ready
to take responsibility...

00:03:52.114 --> 00:03:55.174
Taking so many tranquilizers
isn't healthy, you know.

00:03:57.786 --> 00:04:00.186
I know, but I have a lot of on-the-job stress.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:04.455
Captain, do you understand what I'm telling you?

00:04:04.593 --> 00:04:05.150
Right...

00:04:06.795 --> 00:04:09.787
The Soyokaze is in a state of demotion.

00:04:09.932 --> 00:04:10.523
Right.

00:04:10.799 --> 00:04:12.426
Under these circumstances...

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:14.366
...the captain has to maintain a firm bearing.

00:04:14.537 --> 00:04:16.232
Maintain a firm bearing?

00:04:21.477 --> 00:04:24.469
It's time you started acting like a captain!

00:04:58.581 --> 00:04:59.912
Wha... What's?!

00:05:08.257 --> 00:05:09.656
What just happened?!

00:05:10.926 --> 00:05:13.554
Engine room, come in! Engine room!

00:05:23.272 --> 00:05:24.239
Commander...

00:05:24.773 --> 00:05:26.001
Mine's stopped, too.

00:05:26.275 --> 00:05:28.971
Why would our watches...
No, it couldn't be!

00:05:29.211 --> 00:05:31.475
11:59:59 PM...

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:36.217
Yipes! That's the time when the
old captain killed himself!

00:05:36.318 --> 00:05:38.878
That's ridiculous. Captain, get a hold of yourself!

00:05:39.021 --> 00:05:41.421
Captains can get scared of things, too!

00:05:41.924 --> 00:05:42.913
You're pathetic!

00:05:43.125 --> 00:05:46.295
In his condition, the captain isn't fit...

00:05:46.295 --> 00:05:48.889
...to find out what's happened to the ship.

00:05:50.299 --> 00:05:51.596
Leave this to me!

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:57.065
Well done, Mr. Yamamoto!
Brave decision and fast action!

00:05:57.306 --> 00:05:58.432
You're really great!

00:05:59.108 --> 00:06:02.339
Because I am an officer in the
United Planets Space Force!

00:06:02.745 --> 00:06:05.009
Captain! Give the order for
me to investigate this!

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:08.013
Sure. But you don't know
what might happen to you.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.581
Aren't you afraid, Mr. Yamamoto?

00:06:09.652 --> 00:06:12.780
Whether I'm afraid or not is irrelevant!

00:06:12.955 --> 00:06:14.820
We don't know what's happened to the ship!

00:06:14.923 --> 00:06:16.584
Which is what makes it so scary!

00:06:17.826 --> 00:06:21.262
Captain, are you giving me authority
to investigate this?!

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.561
Or will you do it yourself?
Which will it be?!

00:06:25.234 --> 00:06:28.499
You're hereby authorized.
Check it out thoroughly, okay?

00:06:29.305 --> 00:06:31.432
Thank you very much, captain, sir!

00:06:31.674 --> 00:06:34.939
Now that you've put me in
charge of things, I'll be off.

00:06:49.325 --> 00:06:50.952
Tha- That's impossible!

00:07:00.035 --> 00:07:03.937
Captain! What was that?!
What's going on here?!

00:07:04.006 --> 00:07:06.031
That's what I'd like to know!

00:07:06.375 --> 00:07:08.172
What's going on?

00:07:08.544 --> 00:07:09.875
Someone playing a trick on us?

00:07:10.379 --> 00:07:12.813
No matter. Anyway, they
seem to be experiencing...

00:07:12.881 --> 00:07:15.042
...the human emotion known as "fear."

00:07:15.384 --> 00:07:17.318
For an android like me...

00:07:17.386 --> 00:07:19.047
...it's impossible for me to understand.

00:07:19.888 --> 00:07:23.016
I may be able to analyze Tylor's
mental state, though.

00:07:27.996 --> 00:07:29.896
A voice! Someone's voice!

00:07:30.733 --> 00:07:32.360
Who is in charge?

00:07:33.001 --> 00:07:34.263
Wha- What's that?

00:07:35.037 --> 00:07:38.097
Who is in charge?

00:07:39.742 --> 00:07:42.677
WHO IS IN CHARGE?!

00:07:59.762 --> 00:08:02.230
Who is in charge?

00:08:05.367 --> 00:08:08.063
Are you the one in charge?

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:11.330
I don't know who you are,
but I won't allow you...

00:08:11.407 --> 00:08:13.034
...to scare us with these stupid tricks!

00:08:13.275 --> 00:08:16.267
Are you the one in charge of this ship?

00:08:16.678 --> 00:08:18.236
Who are you?! Show yourself!

00:08:18.614 --> 00:08:21.981
Answer me! Are you in
charge of this ship?!

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:25.019
Yes! I, Yamamoto, have been given...

00:08:25.087 --> 00:08:28.682
...full charge of the destroyer
Soyokaze for the time being!

00:08:29.057 --> 00:08:29.682
Right?

00:08:34.897 --> 00:08:35.955
What's so funny?!

00:08:36.064 --> 00:08:37.998
As you're the one responsible for this ship...

00:08:38.066 --> 00:08:41.001
...then as its commander
you shall know anguish!

00:08:41.069 --> 00:08:44.004
Anguish?! Enough with your theatrics!

00:08:44.106 --> 00:08:46.438
You'd better be ready to stand
before a court-martial!

00:08:51.513 --> 00:08:52.537
Lieutenant Yamamoto!

00:08:57.786 --> 00:08:58.480
This is...

00:09:00.489 --> 00:09:01.615
The elevator?!

00:09:13.035 --> 00:09:14.366
It won't stop!

00:09:14.503 --> 00:09:17.438
You will know well the anguish I felt!

00:09:17.506 --> 00:09:20.600
I am a soldier! I fear nothing!

00:09:20.843 --> 00:09:23.676
Yeah, I'm a soldier! I fear nothing.

00:09:24.513 --> 00:09:26.504
Nothing... at all...

00:09:31.453 --> 00:09:34.445
But, Yuriko, if we go out looking for
Mr. Yamamoto...

00:09:34.523 --> 00:09:36.855
...something bad might happen to us, too.

00:09:37.125 --> 00:09:41.687
Captain, soldiers of the
UPSF don't fear death!

00:09:42.397 --> 00:09:45.093
Abandoning one of our own
would be shameful to us.

00:09:45.167 --> 00:09:48.370
A great man once said "there's
no shame in being shameful."

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:49.894
Who ever said that?

00:09:50.205 --> 00:09:50.728
Me.

00:09:50.873 --> 00:09:52.204
You really are pathetic!

00:09:52.708 --> 00:09:54.801
Captain, if you don't want to come, then don't!

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:58.379
The commander seems to be
much stronger-willed.

00:09:58.914 --> 00:10:00.973
C'mon, Harumi, let's go.

00:10:01.049 --> 00:10:02.607
What? Oh, right.

00:10:03.886 --> 00:10:07.583
I'll come, I'll come! Just don't leave me alone!

00:10:15.564 --> 00:10:17.031
It's stopped! Hm?

00:10:21.169 --> 00:10:22.534
What the?

00:10:31.547 --> 00:10:34.710
What's wrong with all of you?!
What are you doing?!

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:36.875
You're heading for the air lock!
It's a dead end!

00:10:37.152 --> 00:10:39.120
We're sick of it.

00:10:39.187 --> 00:10:42.714
We can't take flying here in disgrace anymore.

00:10:42.891 --> 00:10:44.950
So we're leaving the ship.

00:10:45.193 --> 00:10:46.160
You're what?

00:10:46.595 --> 00:10:50.361
See you on the other side,
Lieutenant Yamamoto.

00:10:50.599 --> 00:10:52.191
The other side?!

00:10:53.902 --> 00:10:55.870
No, stop it! What are you doing?!

00:11:14.189 --> 00:11:15.554
DON'T!

00:11:29.304 --> 00:11:31.670
Damn it, what's going on?!

00:11:32.941 --> 00:11:36.934
Does the captain suffer over his crew's death?!

00:11:37.779 --> 00:11:41.579
Captain? What do you mean?
I'm not the captain!

00:11:41.817 --> 00:11:45.253
Didn't you say before that
you were in charge here?

00:11:45.454 --> 00:11:49.083
Yes, but because the captain
ordered me to investigate this!

00:11:49.458 --> 00:11:52.985
WHAT?! Then who are you?!

00:11:53.662 --> 00:11:56.187
First Officer Lieutenant Yamamoto!

00:11:56.932 --> 00:11:59.924
The first officer also bears
great responsibility!

00:12:00.302 --> 00:12:02.964
Oh, come on! I'm just the first officer!

00:12:06.675 --> 00:12:09.610
You seem to hate your captain.

00:12:09.778 --> 00:12:12.542
Then you shall kill your captain
with your own hands!

00:12:15.884 --> 00:12:16.051
Captain's Quarters

00:12:16.051 --> 00:12:18.353
Captain's Quarters
These are the old captain's quarters, huh?

00:12:18.353 --> 00:12:19.087
Captain's Quarters
Yeah.

00:12:19.087 --> 00:12:20.389
Captain's Quarters
Do we look in here, too?

00:12:20.389 --> 00:12:21.219
Captain's Quarters
Of course!

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:26.593
I'm scared. If we open the door,
his ghost might jump out and!

00:12:26.728 --> 00:12:28.696
Stop being an idiot. We're going in.

00:12:35.871 --> 00:12:37.930
We don't know what'll happen in there!

00:12:38.306 --> 00:12:40.536
See, Captain? No ghosts.

00:13:22.918 --> 00:13:25.478
Captain... Captain Tylor...

00:13:26.054 --> 00:13:27.078
Yuriko!

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:30.615
No fair, fainting before I do!

00:13:39.267 --> 00:13:41.701
Looks like he's been dead for ten years.

00:13:41.903 --> 00:13:45.066
Whoa, you're great, Harumi.
Being a nurse makes you brave.

00:13:45.774 --> 00:13:47.935
You're pretty easily frightened, Captain.

00:13:48.543 --> 00:13:51.137
Well, not just me.
Look what happened to Yuriko.

00:13:51.379 --> 00:13:54.177
I think the commander was
suppressing all her fear.

00:13:54.616 --> 00:13:57.210
Then it just exploded all at once.

00:13:57.719 --> 00:13:59.084
Would you hand me that?

00:13:59.287 --> 00:13:59.912
Right.

00:14:05.393 --> 00:14:08.123
So, you are the captain!

00:14:09.765 --> 00:14:11.357
The corpse speaks!

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:14.194
You're the real captain, right?

00:14:14.436 --> 00:14:19.271
Uh, right. Justy Ueki Tylor, age
twenty. Lieutenant commander.

00:14:20.308 --> 00:14:25.177
Captain Tylor... I, too, was
once captain of the Soyokaze.

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.075
Gee, what a coincidence.

00:14:27.149 --> 00:14:30.607
Since we're both captains of
the same ship, let's be friends.

00:14:31.787 --> 00:14:34.085
The Soyokaze suffered being
downgraded...

00:14:34.156 --> 00:14:36.090
...and her crew couldn't bear the shame.

00:14:36.191 --> 00:14:38.318
So her crew took their lives.

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:41.657
It was all my responsibility! And so...

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:42.389
And so?

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:49.330
Yuriko!

00:14:51.406 --> 00:14:55.775
And so, as the captain of the same ship...

00:14:55.844 --> 00:15:01.805
...you shall know the same
pain of losing your crew!

00:15:02.184 --> 00:15:03.116
No, please!

00:15:09.858 --> 00:15:11.325
What was that, Harumi?

00:15:11.493 --> 00:15:12.960
Just an anesthetic.

00:15:18.834 --> 00:15:20.699
Why, you!

00:15:21.837 --> 00:15:24.806
Harumi, spies are supposed to be tough, right?!

00:15:24.873 --> 00:15:26.033
Do something!

00:15:26.875 --> 00:15:31.369
This feeling I have... Is this
what humans call fear?

00:15:33.481 --> 00:15:34.505
HARUMI!

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:52.061
Must... kill... Tylor...

00:16:01.476 --> 00:16:02.670
Die!

00:16:06.514 --> 00:16:09.278
Huh? Why am I? Where?

00:16:09.517 --> 00:16:11.280
Lieutenant Yamamoto, get a hold of yourself!

00:16:14.923 --> 00:16:16.652
THE GHOST!!!

00:16:21.763 --> 00:16:25.790
Captain! At a time like this,
you must keep a firm bearing!

00:16:25.867 --> 00:16:28.233
Then set a good example for me,
Mr. Yamamoto!

00:16:31.072 --> 00:16:33.097
Agh! Dead end!

00:16:34.509 --> 00:16:35.407
Uh-oh!

00:16:36.912 --> 00:16:40.245
That's the air lock my crew jumped out of.

00:16:40.949 --> 00:16:44.214
Come, jump out like they did!

00:16:44.519 --> 00:16:46.453
But, if we do that, we'll die!

00:16:46.521 --> 00:16:51.515
Yes, die! Know the anguish and
torment of your degraded crew!

00:16:51.693 --> 00:16:52.921
Oh, no!

00:16:53.662 --> 00:16:55.095
You fool!

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:09.070
Agh! My hand! My hand!
I can't control my hand!

00:17:09.177 --> 00:17:11.475
Yes! Open the door!

00:17:13.848 --> 00:17:17.045
Know the anguish I felt!

00:17:20.555 --> 00:17:23.251
Mr. Yamamoto, do something!

00:17:23.358 --> 00:17:26.259
Captain, don't open the air lock!

00:17:26.428 --> 00:17:28.760
Summon your pride as a soldier and resist!

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:32.266
Pride as a soldier my ass! I can't stop myself!

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:35.535
A captain is the most
powerful officer on a ship...

00:17:35.603 --> 00:17:37.332
...meaning he's also the
strongest soldier on board!

00:17:37.605 --> 00:17:40.699
Now take courage and resist! Fight!

00:17:41.009 --> 00:17:43.273
I'll just take being the most powerful officer!

00:17:43.345 --> 00:17:44.812
That's irresponsible!

00:17:45.013 --> 00:17:48.779
At least act like a captain now
that we're about to die!

00:17:48.984 --> 00:17:50.645
Then here's a direct order for you,
Yamamoto!

00:17:50.719 --> 00:17:53.950
Turn around right now and attack that ghost!

00:17:54.022 --> 00:17:55.216
I can't!

00:17:55.357 --> 00:17:57.621
If a captain's the strongest
soldier on board a ship...

00:17:57.692 --> 00:18:00.354
...doesn't that make the first officer
the second strongest?!

00:18:00.695 --> 00:18:03.823
Stop twisting things to your
own advantage, Captain!

00:18:04.032 --> 00:18:06.296
But you just said it yourself,
Lieutenant!

00:18:06.568 --> 00:18:08.968
You have a lot of pride as a soldier, right?

00:18:09.037 --> 00:18:12.666
Now screw up your courage and
fight that ghost! That's an order!

00:18:13.041 --> 00:18:17.307
Can anyone be that irresponsible?!
Don't you care about your crew?!

00:18:17.545 --> 00:18:20.309
Well, doesn't the crew care about its captain?!

00:18:20.415 --> 00:18:23.316
Damn it, I should've killed you back there!

00:18:23.585 --> 00:18:25.553
Oh, so you DID know what you were doing!

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:29.112
Are you two really in charge of this ship?

00:18:34.329 --> 00:18:35.956
You're pathetic!

00:18:36.398 --> 00:18:38.332
What would be the point of...

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.994
...killing anyone as irresponsible as you two?

00:18:41.269 --> 00:18:42.736
You're ridiculous!

00:18:51.346 --> 00:18:53.143
Whew... Looks like we're safe.

00:18:53.415 --> 00:18:56.248
He was irresponsible enough to disgust a ghost.

00:18:56.418 --> 00:18:58.716
Don't put all the blame on me,
Lieutenant.

00:18:59.754 --> 00:19:02.655
Hm? We're back at the old captain's quarters.

00:19:02.724 --> 00:19:04.385
Oh, Yuriko!

00:19:07.996 --> 00:19:09.657
Thank goodness. You're awake.

00:19:30.452 --> 00:19:32.716
Maybe it was a
group hallucination.

00:19:32.921 --> 00:19:34.718
That's the only thing I can think of.

00:19:34.789 --> 00:19:37.917
Maybe, but that was one heck of
a realistic hallucination.

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:43.090
I'm an android, and not
programmed to feel fear.

00:19:43.965 --> 00:19:46.627
But, back there, I!

00:19:50.138 --> 00:19:52.402
Well, my friends on the Soyokaze,
it's been a while.

00:19:52.774 --> 00:19:54.207
Admiral Fuji!

00:19:54.576 --> 00:19:55.804
Anything unusual out there?

00:19:56.010 --> 00:20:00.276
Unusual? Boy, did you pick
a great time to call!

00:20:00.715 --> 00:20:02.080
You see, just now we...

00:20:02.150 --> 00:20:04.414
Captain! Don't tell him
about the hallucination!

00:20:04.519 --> 00:20:05.383
Huh? Why?

00:20:05.453 --> 00:20:07.387
Any talk about group hallucinations...

00:20:07.455 --> 00:20:10.424
...will send us further and
further from the front line.

00:20:10.492 --> 00:20:12.255
Lieutenant Yamamoto's right!

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:13.590
You guys are no fun.

00:20:14.496 --> 00:20:16.361
Hey! What are you three muttering about?!

00:20:16.431 --> 00:20:19.127
Oh, nothing! Nothing at all, sir!

00:20:21.503 --> 00:20:23.164
What the?! That's!

00:20:27.842 --> 00:20:30.538
Commander Tylor, where did
you get that corncob pipe?!

00:20:30.745 --> 00:20:34.875
Oh, this? Uh, how I got it is a secret.

00:20:35.183 --> 00:20:37.708
But it has nothing to do with
the ship's old captain!

00:20:37.819 --> 00:20:38.945
Captain, no!

00:20:40.155 --> 00:20:41.782
How much does he know?

00:20:42.056 --> 00:20:43.717
Does he know what I did to the Soyokaze?

00:20:44.092 --> 00:20:46.754
But doesn't having this prove
it isn't just a rumor...

00:20:46.828 --> 00:20:49.023
...and that it all really happened?

00:20:49.197 --> 00:20:50.789
Just don't tell him!

00:20:51.199 --> 00:20:54.293
By the way, what can we do for you,
Admiral Fuji?

00:20:54.802 --> 00:20:57.134
If you have any missions for me...

00:20:57.405 --> 00:21:00.670
...I stand ready to complete them with
a soldier's pride and courage!

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:04.440
Is he trying to make a deal with me?

00:21:05.813 --> 00:21:07.303
Hm? Something wrong?

00:21:07.448 --> 00:21:11.976
Uh, that is, I have a special
mission for the Soyokaze!

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:14.518
You're to break off your current duty...

00:21:14.589 --> 00:21:17.149
...and rendezvous with the
UPSF main fleet at once!

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:19.590
What's going on?

00:21:19.694 --> 00:21:20.328
I don't know.

00:21:20.328 --> 00:21:24.788
Is that clear? You heard the orders.
Now get going, people.

00:21:26.901 --> 00:21:28.102
What just happened?

00:21:28.102 --> 00:21:30.127
I think he just rescinded the ship's downgrade.

00:21:30.238 --> 00:21:31.432
Rescinded the downgrade?

00:21:39.914 --> 00:21:40.248
All right! We did it!

00:21:40.248 --> 00:21:42.910
Hooray!
All right! We did it!

00:22:12.513 --> 00:22:13.502
The Irresponsible Captain Tylor
Next Episode

00:22:15.149 --> 00:22:19.017
Heroes of old say "Strength leads to
victory on the battlefield."

00:22:19.187 --> 00:22:22.554
But Tylor says "Luck is
what leads to victory!"

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:24.783
Next time, "Be Prepared,
Be Smart, or Be Lucky."

00:22:25.026 --> 00:22:25.890
Watch for it.

00:22:26.661 --> 00:22:28.492
Filming is Job 1!
Working hard for those who demand
the finest in image and sound

00:22:39.707 --> 00:22:42.810
All he has to do is just...
Machi o Aitsu ga Aruiteru dake de

00:22:42.810 --> 00:22:45.904
...walk around downtown.
Machi o Aitsu ga Aruiteru dake de

00:22:46.414 --> 00:22:49.884
He's a playful man who catches...
Nandemo Ki o Hiku Ochame na Yatsu sa

00:22:49.884 --> 00:22:52.717
...the eyes of all who he meets.
Nandemo Ki o Hiku Ochame na Yatsu sa

00:22:53.221 --> 00:22:56.057
Oh! That's why, you see...
Aa, Dakara sa Sou Kore kara Shuyaku

00:22:56.057 --> 00:22:59.857
...he'll be our hero from now on.
Aa, Dakara sa Sou Kore kara Shuyaku

00:23:00.662 --> 00:23:03.031
So, let's begin...
Henshin Byouyomi o Shite yo!

00:23:03.031 --> 00:23:06.865
...the countdown for the change!
Henshin Byouyomi o Shite yo!

00:23:10.338 --> 00:23:13.136
Take a deep breath, and one two.
12345 Ikizugi o One Two

00:23:14.275 --> 00:23:16.611
Now stride out...
Saa Kore kara Kuridasou

00:23:16.611 --> 00:23:19.774
...with your head held high.
Saa Kore kara Kuridasou

00:23:19.914 --> 00:23:23.645
Downtown Dance
